WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.240
Fall is fast approaching, and you know what
that means: cooler weather, back to school

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.800
sales, and an updated Netflix lineup to keep
you indoors and away from it all.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.540
September's heralding a galaxy's worth of
new programming for the streaming service.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.200
On the Netflix originals side, we're looking
forward to new seasons of Bojack Horseman

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.120
and Narcos, plus a handful of Netflix original
movies.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:22.500
And an end-of-summer binge wouldn't be complete
without the upcoming true-crime satire American

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Vandal.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.740
Here's an in-depth look at everything coming
to Netflix in September 2017.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.060
Narcos Season 3

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.390
The DEA is setting its sights on a new drug
lord in the third season of its addicting

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.620
crime drama Narcos.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.239
Where the first two seasons fixated on Colombian
kingpin Pablo Escobar, the newest season will

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.640
raise the stakes even higher as the DEA launches
its operation against the Cali Cartel.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:49.079
Pedro Pascal returns as DEA agent Javier Pena,
delivering more of the same gripping, real-life

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.020
drama that catapulted the first two seasons
to critical acclaim.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.120
Get ready to binge September 1.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:55.540
Little Evil

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.680
Call us crazy, but Little Evil looks like
it just may be one of the best movies of 2017.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.780
Starring Adam Scott and Evangeline Lilly,
and written and directed by Tucker and Dale

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.790
vs Evil's Eli Craig, Little Evil is a horror
comedy about a newly married man who may just

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:11.720
be the new stepdad to the antichrist.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.420
Get set for big, dark laughs when Little Evil
hits on September 1.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.100
Resurface

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.240
With gorgeous visuals and a heartfelt message
about veterans struggling to find their place

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.760
in the world, Resurface documents the journey
of a suicidal ex-soldier who uses surfing

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.140
as a way to escape his physical and emotional
pain.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.100
Along the way, he finds a community of like-minded
veterans searching for peace among the waves.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.580
Experience the journey September 1.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.720
Marc Maron: Too Real

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.460
Comedian Marc Maron has been making the world
laugh for years with his WTF podcast, and

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.180
he's recently experienced a resurgence on
Netflix thanks to his role on Glow.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.759
Now, he's dishing out laughs with a brand
new stand-up comedy special, Too Real.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:50.680
Look for it September 5.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.380
Bojack Horseman : Season 4

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.620
Bojack's back, and this time it's serious.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:57.160
Sometimes.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.800
Other times, it's bound to be funny, heartwarming,
tear-jerking, and poignant.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.920
Maybe a bunch of those all at once, because
you never know what you're going to pull out

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:04.580
of that bag.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.940
Netflix has been pretty quiet about the details
for the fourth season of Bojack Horseman,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.880
so we'll just have to wait for Bojack's return
on September 8.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.640
#REALITYHIGH

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.780
Nobody likes meeting their partner's ex, but
things get extra hairy when that ex happens

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.240
to be a social media starlet who's out for
your blood.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:24.760
#REALITYHIGH is a Netflix original comedy
starring Kate Walsh, Anne Winters, and John

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:25.640
Michael Higgins.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.000
It premieres September 8.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.340
Greenhouse Academy: Season 1

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.640
Following two siblings at a boarding school
in California who find themselves in the middle

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:38.769
of a mystery, Greenhouse Academy stars Heartland's
Jessica Amlee and newcomer Finn Roberts.

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:40.260
Check out the first season on September 8.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.600
The Confession Tapes: Season 1

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.810
The first season of Netflix's documentary
series The Confession Tapes drops September

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.740
8, focusing on convicted murderers who claim
to be innocent.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.220
If The Confession Tapes is received half as
well as Making a Murderer, it may be destined

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.140
to become a new true crime classic.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.480
Fire Chasers: Season 1

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.020
What if your day job put you at risk of being
engulfed in flames on a regular basis?

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:08.260
From the producers of Deadliest Catch, Fire
Chasers follows the firefighters who go face-to-face

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.820
with California's deadly wildfires to protect
the people in the fire's path.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.420
Check it out on September 8.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.000
Jeff Dunham: Relative Disaster

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:20.860
Taped at a live show in Ireland, Relative
Disaster is chock full of Jeff Dunham's trademark

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.720
mash-up of humor and ventriloquism.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.040
Get ready for all-new jokes, all-new hijinks,
and, of course, all-new puppets on September

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:27.540
12.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.340
Strong Island

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.840
On September 15, Netflix is adding to their
docu-drama selection with Strong Island, a

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.360
powerful look into murder and racism on Long
Island during the early '90s.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:42.320
Diving into the real-life story of a young
African-American who was murdered, and the

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.860
justice system that failed his family, Strong
Island isn't for the faint-hearted.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:50.840
Strong Island is one of the most intimately
moving portraits of racism in recent memory.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.980
Strap in, because these are stormy seas.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.280
And on the other end of the spectrum, we have...

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.320
American Vandal: Season 1

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.079
The trailer for Netflix's American Vandal
plays this story of mystery and true crime

00:04:02.079 --> 00:04:07.640
hilariously straight despite its simple premise:
Someone at Hanover High School, someone nefarious,

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.640
defaced the school with a ton of hand-drawn
dongs.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.300
It's the biggest mystery on campus — who
doodled the doodles?

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.950
Will the mystery vandal ever be brought to
justice?

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:19.060
And more importantly, will the wrong man pay
the price for the peters?

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.540
Find out on September 15.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.840
First They Killed My Father

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:28.220
Directed by Angelina Jolie, First They Killed
My Father is a historical docu-drama set during

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.340
the time of the Khmer Rouge regime in Cambodia.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.460
The story is told from the perspective of
a five-year-old girl struggling to survive

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:39.200
the harsh regime, promising a gripping, heartfelt
tale of courage and the strength of the human

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:39.700
spirit.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.320
First They Killed My Father premieres September
15.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.560
Jerry Before Seinfeld

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.400
You don't become the world's highest paid
comedian by sitting back and resting on your

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.900
fame, and Jerry Seinfeld is back in the saddle
with a brand new stand-up special.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.840
The first release in Seinfeld's $100 million,
two-special deal with Netflix, Jerry Before

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.841
Seinfeld is, as the name suggests, all about
the early years in Seinfeld's career, before

00:05:01.841 --> 00:05:03.440
the hit show, and before the fame.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.900
Check it out when it hits Netflix on September
19.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.420
Fuller House: Season 3

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:14.620
Way back on September 22, 1987, the first
episode of Full House premiered on ABC and

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.300
introduced the world to the Tanner family.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.780
Now, the third season of the popular Netflix
sequel series, Fuller House, is premiering

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:25.860
exactly 30 years later, as revealed by actress
Candace Cameron Bure in an Instagram post.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.949
Only the first nine episodes are premiering
on Netflix on September 22, while the second

00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:33.880
half of the season will likely hit in late
2017 or early 2018.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.540
Jack Whitehall: Travels with My Father

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.180
You may know Jack Whitehall from his stand-up
comedy or from the comedy series Fresh Meat.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:45.080
The British comedian joins the Netflix roster
this month with Travels with My Father.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.139
The series follows Whitehall and his dad as
they travel around Europe and try to bond

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.759
— which goes about as well as you'd expect
with a goofball and a grumpy old man.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.540
"A priest would not say you're such a little
s---, he'd probably forgive me"

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.100
"He'd probably tell you to f--- off."

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.040
Look for it on September 22.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.660
Terrace House: Aloha State: Part 4

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:05.700
If you haven't seen Netflix's original reality
series Terrace House, it's definitely worth

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:06.200
a watch.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.380
In the vein of reality mainstays like The
Real World, the show throws a group of strangers

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.600
into a house together and turns on the cameras.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:17.360
While the previous seasons took place in Japan,
Aloha State moves the action to sunny Hawaii.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.860
Dig in for Part 4 on September 26.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:21.160
Gerald's Game

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:26.080
Adapted from the Stephen King novel of the
same name, Gerald's Game stars Carla Gugino

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:30.139
and Bruce Greenwood as Jessie and Gerald,
a husband and wife whose vacation soon takes

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.060
a turn for the worse.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.580
Gerald's Game is directed by Mike Flanagan,
who's already garnered some serious street

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:38.380
cred in the horror genre with his previous
films like Hush and Oculus.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:39.600
Check it out on September 29.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.700
Our Souls at Night

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:46.580
Robert Redford and Jane Fonda star in Our
Souls at Night as two elderly neighbors who

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:49.520
form an unexpected bond years after their
spouses have died.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:53.420
The film is based on a novel by Kent Haruf,
and the story it tells is a poignant glimpse

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:54.720
of love and loss.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.620
Queue it up on September 29, and keep a tissue
handy.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.660
Big Mouth: Season 1

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:04.979
Netflix calls Big Mouth "a 10-episode, half-hour
edgy adult animated comedy from real-life

00:07:04.979 --> 00:07:09.020
best friends Nick Kroll and Andrew Goldberg
about the glorious nightmare that is teenaged

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:09.520
puberty."

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:13.860
If the pre-release clips are any indication,
it'll definitely be an odd show, but it has

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:15.660
plenty of comedy heavyweights behind it.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:20.100
Other voice actors tied to the show include
Maya Rudolph, Jordan Peele, Fred Armisen,

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:20.800
and Jenny Slate.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.920
Big Mouth premieres on September 29.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:25.340
Club de Cuervos : Season 3

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:29.520
This comedy series marked Netflix's first
Spanish original show when the streaming service

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:33.180
released the first season in 2015, and it
turned out to be a pretty good move.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.800
With an 80% rating on Rotten Tomatoes, the
first two seasons were quick to pull in fans.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:41.740
And now would be a good time to go rewatch
those seasons, because the third one is dropping

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:42.660
on September 29.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.700
The Magic School Bus Rides Again: Season 1

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:51.060
Who could forget The Magic School Bus, the
classic '90s show that entertained and educated?

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:55.070
Well, hold onto your inner child, because
The Magic School Bus is getting a reboot.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:58.840
According to Netflix, the new show will follow
Miss Frizzle's sister, and is slated for a

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.240
September 29 release.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:01.560
New Movies

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:05.720
Netflix is kicking off the month with a ton
of new movies along with a handful of old

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:06.220
favorites.

00:08:06.729 --> 00:08:10.860
Highlights include the criminally underrated
Brazilian crime drama City of God, Martin

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:15.480
Scorsese's hard-hitting epic Gangs of New
York, and Quentin Tarantino's stylish Pulp

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:17.740
Fiction, all of which drop on September 1.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:22.440
For new releases, keep an eye out for the
upcoming 2017 sci-fi action thriller Alien

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.940
Arrival, about a soldier marooned on an alien
moon.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:26.419
Look for it September 23.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:30.340
And you better believe you'll be able to get
your shark fix this month, with the entire

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:35.010
Jaws franchise and Deep Blue Sea also hitting
Netflix on the first of the month.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:38.220
It's the perfect time for a movie marathon...if
the sharks will let you.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:47.400
And if you want some good jokes, Netflix is
loading up with All Star Comedy Jam stand-up

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.860
specials on September 1.

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:53.700
If stand-up's not your thing, tune into Absolutely
Anything, starring Simon Pegg and featuring

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:58.160
the voices of Robin Williams and members of
the Monty Python crew, on September 27.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.380
New documentary releases include Facing Darkness,
coming September 5, and Ghost of the Mountains,

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.280
available for streaming on September 13.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:09.060
And if you love music, you can't miss out
on George Harrison: Living in the Material

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:12.880
World, an in-depth look into the life and
music of the former Beatle, directed by Martin

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:13.660
Scorsese.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.420
Look for that on September 15.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:19.180
Finally, what's cooler weather without a cozy
family movie night?

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:23.600
Pop some popcorn and settle in with the kids,
because Netflix is boosting their Disney selection

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.930
this September with the addition of Mulan
and Hercules on the 1st, Pocahontas on the

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:30.000
14th, and Beauty and the Beast on the 19th.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.280
New Television

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:36.760
Bingeing on your favorite shows will be easier
than ever this month, with a new season of

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:41.790
The Blacklist hitting on September 7, The
Walking Dead on the 8th, Gotham on the 21st,

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.360
and Dark Matter on the 25th of the month..

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:48.700
And keep an eye out for Final Fantasy XIV:
Daddy of Light, a quirky Japanese series which

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:53.140
chronicles a father and son bonding over — you
guessed it — Final Fantasy.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:54.980
Now that's an intriguing premise.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:59.240
For the international crowd, Netflix is bringing
on Star Trek: Discovery, the first Star Trek

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.200
show since Star Trek: Enterprise wrapped back
in 2005.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:06.380
Discovery follows the crew of a new ship called
the Discovery, and it's set about 10 years

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:08.320
before the events of The Original Series.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.760
Set your phasers to fun on September 25.

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:13.580
Well, everywhere except the US and Canada,
that is.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:15.900
"Most illogical."

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:17.520
Thanks for watching!

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.000
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.200
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

